  "characterization": "lodging",
  "holding_summary": "A widow who is head of a family and supports herself and her children by keeping boarders, and who owns two adjoining town lots with a building on each (living in one, with rooms in the other occupied by boarders or rented out), may claim both lots as her homestead since both were purchased for homestead purposes. The homestead exemption was upheld against a forced sale despite the boarding and rental use of the second building.",
